5. REPAIR OF THE THREE RE-ASSEMBLED INPUTS IN tb/base.7z
------------------------------------------------------------------------
base.7z shipped re-assembled copies of lib/web51_80.obj, lib/web51_23.obj
and lib/libw80.a. A re-assembly by the port's own gas could not write the
processor-specific section index of an external memory-space common, so
each of those symbols came out as a plain SHN_COMMON and the linker then
allocated it in byte-addressed .bss. Symbol-table census, 2001 original
against the copy base.7z carried:

  lib/web51_80.obj  0xff02 x1, 0xff06 x6            ->  SHN_COMMON x9
  lib/web51_23.obj  0xff02 x1, 0xff06 x8            ->  SHN_COMMON x12
  lib/libw80.a      0xff00 x11, 0xff02 x2,
                    0xff03 x2, 0xff06 x21           ->  SHN_COMMON x46

The three were replaced by conversions of the 2001 originals, which
tb/base2001.7z carries and whose hashes are the section 1 block above.
Loose objects go through the two-step pipeline; the archive goes through
tb/i51elf_ar.py, which runs the same two steps on every member and then
uppercases the armap and writes deterministic ar headers.

  py tb/i51elf_le2be.py  <2001>/lib/web51_80.obj  w80.le2be
  py tb/i51elf_sym_uc.py w80.le2be               lib/web51_80.obj
  py tb/i51elf_le2be.py  <2001>/lib/web51_23.obj  w23.le2be
  py tb/i51elf_sym_uc.py w23.le2be               lib/web51_23.obj
  py tb/i51elf_ar.py     <2001>/lib/libw80.a      lib/libw80.a

Conversion carries every index through unchanged, verified by re-running
the census on the output. The pipeline is checked against the three
archives base.7z already held in converted form: tb/i51elf_ar.py
reproduces lib/libk80.a, lib/libk23.a and lib/libw23.a from their
base2001.7z originals byte-for-byte. The two loose objects come out
byte-identical to staged/lib/web51_80.obj and staged/lib/web51_23.obj
recorded in section 2.

